About this repository
This repository is intended to support the teaching and learning of Machine Learning for students and faculty members of DBATU-affiliated institutes. It brings together course-aligned study material, Python programs, Jupyter notebooks, and practical exercises.
The examples are intended to help learners understand machine learning concepts through implementation, experimentation, visualisation and model evaluation. Faculty members may use the resources for classroom demonstrations, laboratory sessions and supplementary learning.
Please note: This is an independently maintained educational resource. It is not an official DBATU website, repository or publication. 

How students can use this repository
1.	Read the aim and problem statement of the experiment.
2.	Understand the code before executing it.
3.	Run the notebook or program step by step.
4.	Observe the output, graphs and evaluation measures.
5.	Experiment with different inputs, parameters and datasets.
6.	Write observations and results in your own words.
7.  students can directly print their updated experiments with CRL+P. 
8.	Follow the practical journal and submission instructions of your
institute.

Use these resources to learn and practise. Do not submit copied work as
your own; follow your institute's academic integrity requirements.
